The  system call submits a completed BSM audit record to the sys‐
tem audit log.  The argument is a pointer to the  specific  event
to  be  recorded and is the size in bytes of the data to be writ‐
ten.  The system call will fail and the data  never  written  if:
The  argument  is  beyond  the  allocated  address  space  of the
process.  The token ID is invalid or is larger than  The  process
does  not  have  sufficient permission to complete the operation.
